{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558852522,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf5cb73ffeyTurLwJkKK3EkO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d40afbb2002jf5bxASF9EZDys","sessionID":"ses_e2bf5cb73ffeyTurLwJkKK3EkO","messageID":"msg_1d40ae82d001BQ4RKMwWyixZD8","type":"tool","id":"call_43545673882e4db9a1590791","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml","offset":140,"limit":45},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml, lines 140-184\n140: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n141: execution:\n142:   steps:\n143:     - \"Run upstream_assets.runtime_mirrors with --check. Covers the cursor/devin agent, command and skill symlink trees, all four hook discovery mirrors and the .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ links into the hook library. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n144:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_agents with --check. Covers the generated .codex/agents/*.toml. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n145:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .codex/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n146:     - \"Run upstream_assets.agent_roster. Covers roster coverage across all five surfaces and rejects a real file where a symlink belongs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error (bad argument, canonical dir missing, or crash).\"\n147:     - \"Run upstream_assets.agent_body_parity with --all. Compares each agent body across the runtime trees; same-file mirrors and non-comparable formats are reported, not counted as matches. Exit 0 = all comparable mirrors in sync, 1 = drift or comparison failure, 2 = checker invocation error (unknown option), 3 = not checkable (frontmatter parser unavailable).\"\n148:     - \"Run upstream_assets.command_catalog. Compare command frontmatter with the root and family indexes and hub metadata. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error.\"\n149:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_hooks_installer with --check --allow-worktree. Covers the user-global ~/.codex/hooks.json against the repo's .codex/hooks.json, including orphaned entries whose .skilled adapter no longer exists on disk. Explicit OK output = in sync; a drift report = drift; refusal, error, or missing affirmative output = error.\"\n150:     - 'Run upstream_assets.codex_hook_approval with --root \"$PWD\". Covers the Codex approval that lets the project advisor hook run at all, since Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. PASS = in sync. WARN sets STATUS to WARN and shows the repair line it prints without counting as drift. SKIP leaves STATUS unchanged. Exit 0 = approved or no Codex hooks file, 1 = absent or unapproved, 2 = checker error.'\n151:     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_agents with --check. Covers the generated .pi/agents/*.md. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n152:     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .pi/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n153:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_skills, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/skills/ links. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n154:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_prompts, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/prompts/*.md files. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n155:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_agents, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/agents/*.patch.yml files. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n156:     - \"For each row in hook_adapter_fallback_health_checks, run its file_exists check (a plain path-existence read, no execution of the adapter or the shell command that wraps it). Collect every row whose path does not resolve as a degraded hook adapter, keyed by host:event:path.\"\n157:     - \"Aggregate: report each surface with its own verdict rather than a single pass/fail, so the operator learns which mirror moved.\"\n158: \n159: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n160: # OUTPUT\n161: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n162: output: |\n163:   STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync, or n/a for a DSH row while its runtime tree is absent, and the\n164:   Codex hook approval check reports in sync or skip.\n165:   STATUS=WARN when the Codex hook approval check reports an unapproved or absent advisor entry and no checker\n166:   reports drift: show its lines, including the repair line it prints, without adding a drift surface.\n167:   STATUS=DRIFT when any checker reports drift, listing each drifting surface and the repair command for it:\n168:     runtime mirrors  -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\n169:     codex agents     -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs\n170:     codex prompts    -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\n171:     codex hooks      -> node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\n172:     agent body parity (.skilled/bin/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs) -> .claude/agents is a hand-maintained real-file mirror; update both its .skilled source and Claude twin, then run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs for .codex/agents, node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs for .pi/agents, and node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs for the .cursor and .devin links\n173:     pi agents        -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\n174:     pi prompts       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\n175:     dsh skills       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs\n176:     dsh prompts      -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs\n177:     dsh agents       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs\n178:     command catalog  -> update the root and family indexes, group counts, and hub metadata from command frontmatter\n179:   While .dsh/ is absent the three DSH rows read n/a (no .dsh/ tree), never in sync, and leave\n180:   STATUS unchanged: the mirror does not exist yet, and this run never creates it. Their repair lines are the generators without --check, run once the tree exists.\n181:   The agent roster check has no generator. Its drift is repaired by the runtime-mirrors generator or by hand\n182:   for the authored surfaces (.skilled/agents and .claude/agents).\n183:   Hook CONFIG STRUCTURE is deliberately out of scope for mirroring: the four runtimes use incompatible event\n184:   vocabularies and entry shapes, so those files are hand-authored per runtime and cannot be mirror-checked\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 185]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml, lines 140-184\n140: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n141: execution:\n142:   steps:\n143:     - \"Run upstream_assets.runtime_mirrors with --check. Covers the cursor/devin agent, command and skill symlink trees, all four hook discovery mirrors and the .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ links into the hook library. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n144:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_agents with --check. Covers the generated .codex/agents/*.toml. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n145:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .codex/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n146:     - \"Run upstream_assets.agent_roster. Covers roster coverage across all five surfaces and rejects a real file where a symlink belongs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error (bad argument, canonical dir missing, or crash).\"\n147:     - \"Run upstream_assets.agent_body_parity with --all. Compares each agent body across the runtime trees; same-file mirrors and non-comparable formats are reported, not counted as matches. Exit 0 = all comparable mirrors in sync, 1 = drift or comparison failure, 2 = checker invocation error (unknown option), 3 = not checkable (frontmatter parser unavailable).\"\n148:     - \"Run upstream_assets.command_catalog. Compare command frontmatter with the root and family indexes and hub metadata. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error.\"\n149:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_hooks_installer with --check --allow-worktree. Covers the user-global ~/.codex/hooks.json against the repo's .codex/hooks.json, including orphaned entries whose .skilled adapter no longer exists on disk. Explicit OK output = in sync; a drift report = drift; refusal, error, or missing affirmative output = error.\"\n150:     - 'Run upstream_assets.codex_hook_approval with --root \"$PWD\". Covers the Codex approval that lets the project advisor hook run at all, since Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. PASS = in sync. WARN sets STATUS to WARN and shows the repair line it prints without counting as drift. SKIP leaves STATUS unchanged. Exit 0 = approved or no Codex hooks file, 1 = absent or unapproved, 2 = checker error.'\n151:     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_agents with --check. Covers the generated .pi/agents/*.md. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n152:     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .pi/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n153:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_skills, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/skills/ links. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n154:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_prompts, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/prompts/*.md files. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n155:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_agents, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/agents/*.patch.yml files. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n156:     - \"For each row in hook_adapter_fallback_health_checks, run its file_exists check (a plain path-existence read, no execution of the adapter or the shell command that wraps it). Collect every row whose path does not resolve as a degraded hook adapter, keyed by host:event:path.\"\n157:     - \"Aggregate: report each surface with its own verdict rather than a single pass/fail, so the operator learns which mirror moved.\"\n158: \n159: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n160: # OUTPUT\n161: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n162: output: |\n163:   STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync, or n/a for a DSH row while its runtime tree is absent, and the\n164:   Codex hook approval check reports in sync or skip.\n165:   STATUS=WARN when the Codex hook approval check reports an unapproved or absent advisor entry and no checker\n166:   reports drift: show its lines, including the repair line it prints, without adding a drift surface.\n167:   STATUS=DRIFT when any checker reports drift, listing each drifting surface and the repair command for it:\n168:     runtime mirrors  -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\n169:     codex agents     -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs\n170:     codex prompts    -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\n171:     codex hooks      -> node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\n172:     agent body parity (.skilled/bin/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs) -> .claude/agents is a hand-maintained real-file mirror; update both its .skilled source and Claude twin, then run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs for .codex/agents, node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs for .pi/agents, and node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs for the .cursor and .devin links\n173:     pi agents        -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\n174:     pi prompts       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\n175:     dsh skills       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs\n176:     dsh prompts      -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs\n177:     dsh agents       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs\n178:     command catalog  -> update the root and family indexes, group counts, and hub metadata from command frontmatter\n179:   While .dsh/ is absent the three DSH rows read n/a (no .dsh/ tree), never in sync, and leave\n180:   STATUS unchanged: the mirror does not exist yet, and this run never creates it. Their repair lines are the generators without --check, run once the tree exists.\n181:   The agent roster check has no generator. Its drift is repaired by the runtime-mirrors generator or by hand\n182:   for the authored surfaces (.skilled/agents and .claude/agents).\n183:   Hook CONFIG STRUCTURE is deliberately out of scope for mirroring: the four runtimes use incompatible event\n184:   vocabularies and entry shapes, so those files are hand-authored per runtime and cannot be mirror-checked\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 185]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml\",\"offset\":140,\"limit\":45}"},"time":{"start":1794558852018,"end":1794558852522}}}}
