{"type":"text","timestamp":1794558925605,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf5cb73ffeyTurLwJkKK3EkO","part":{"id":"prt_1d40c0bc0001ZdON95cjW0W7kA","sessionID":"ses_e2bf5cb73ffeyTurLwJkKK3EkO","messageID":"msg_1d40c041e00119L8mj55fXKwsE","type":"text","text":"T030 complete.\n\n## Files written\n\n1. `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs`\n   - Added `an absent advisor entry prints the repair that creates it`: a root whose `.codex/hooks.json` has only a `UserPromptSubmit` entry running another script, asserting exit 1, the exact repair line in text output, and the same text in the `--json` `repair` field.\n\n2. `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`\n   - The absent branch now builds the repair (`repair: copy the advisor UserPromptSubmit entry from the Skilled checkout's .codex/hooks.json into <hooksFile>, then approve it with /hooks in a Codex session`), adds it to the JSON verdict, and prints it after the `WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent` line. Its existing exit 1 is unchanged, and the read-only, no-hash policy in the header still holds.\n\n## Verify output\n\nBefore the change, the new case failed on `actual: 'WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent\\n'` versus the expected WARN plus repair line. After:\n\n```\n$ node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs\nNT exit: 0\nℹ tests 5\nℹ pass 5\nℹ fail 0\n\n$ rg -c \"including the repair line it prints\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml\n1\nrg exit: 0\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- The diff for `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` also contains pre-existing uncommitted changes from the T029 lane (`startsWith('-')` guard and its comment). I left them untouched.\n- `doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml` was not edited. Its line 166 already carries the \"including the repair line it prints\" promise, which this change now fulfils.\n- Checkbox not ticked, no other files changed, no git state touched.","time":{"start":1794558921664,"end":1794558925605}}}
